    "question": {
      ":question/id": "5b1e6461-4662-5ed4-8cde-319bf158b165",
      ":question/problem": "![](images/57/57fd993fac384d9dd76399aa35eec0d9113afeb3c1d24c0a5349d7b4b99df4f1.png)\n\nLet $A(-16, 4)$ and $B(12, 0)$. Find $|\\overrightarrow{AB}|$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{OA} &= a = - 16 i + 4 j, \\\\\n\\overrightarrow{OB} &= b = 12 i.\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpressing $\\overrightarrow{AB}$ as the difference of position vectors, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\overrightarrow{AB} &= \\overrightarrow{OB} - \\overrightarrow{OA} \\\\\n&= b - a \\\\\n&= (12 i) - (- 16 i + 4 j) \\\\\n&= 28 i - 4 j\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, using the formula for the magnitude of a vector, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n|\\overrightarrow{AB}| &= \\sqrt{(28)^{2} + (-4)^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{784 + 16} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{800} \\\\\n&= 20 \\sqrt{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/requires-calculator": false,
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
